   "evidence": "The library already has `ContractionSemigroup.ofMultiplication_apply` and `ofMultiplication_apply_apply_apply` (Multiplication/Basic.lean:223, 241), but nothing in this file specializes them to `semigroup`. `resolvent_eq_smul_id` also starts by unfolding with `rw [semigroup, ...]`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Examples/Analysis/Semigroups/Resolvent.lean",
   "fix": "Add `@[simp] theorem semigroup_apply (t : \u211d\u22650) : semigroup t = Real.exp (-(t : \u211d)) \u2022 ContinuousLinearMap.id \u211d Space`, proved from `ContractionSemigroup.ofMultiplication_apply_apply_apply`. Optionally also add a pointwise `semigroup_apply_apply`.",
   "issue": "`semigroup` is public and its docstring says it multiplies every function by `exp (-t)`, but no lemma states this. The only characterizations are `eq_ofBounded` (equality of semigroups) and the resolvent formula, so getting `semigroup t` requires `rw [semigroup]` plus the library lemmas.",
